.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-PAIR-CLOCK 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-pair\-clock \- experimentally change a base/EXP pair's hardware rate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B octa-pair-clock --experimental
.I RATE BASE_CARD BASE_SERIAL EXP_CARD EXP_SERIAL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run as the regular device user after all audio servers and applications have
released both units. Cards are native ALSA identifiers, not PCM plugin names.
The base must be USB 0582:0120, the expansion 0582:0121, and both selected serials
must match the opened card slots. Empty or duplicate serials are rejected.
.PP
Connect EXP coaxial output to base coaxial input and select DIGITAL AUTO on the
base. The base must report an active external clock and EXP must be internally
clocked. Both must initially report the same supported rate.
.PP
Supported rates are 44100, 48000 and 96000 Hz. This command reserves capture and
playback on both cards, prepares only EXP capture at the exact requested rate,
and requires two coherent status snapshots from both units. It does not start
or transfer PCM samples. The original module's hardware rate handshake is used;
no guessed clock-source command is sent.
.PP
After an uncertain change, failure or SIGINT/SIGTERM requests restoration of the
previous rate while retaining all reservations. Recovery checks the selected
EXP identity and master role again, and verifies both units. Forced termination
cannot guarantee recovery. Settling and recovery are each limited to forty polls
and an eight-second deadline; an individual ALSA operation can add its own wait.
.PP
JSON output distinguishes a successful change, failure before mutation, verified
recovery and failed recovery. A recovered failure still returns an error.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Experimental developer interface. Real two-unit clock transitions and streaming
remain unverified. This command does not pause or restore an audio server, update
aggregate configuration, or establish measured phase/clock quality. The GUI and
octa-aggregate do not yet invoke it. Release both units explicitly before use.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on verified success, 1 on failure, 2 on invalid command syntax or root use.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR octa-aggregate (1),
.BR octa-status (1)
